WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:10.340 --> 00:00:12.840
Good morning, John. It's Tuesday March 20th

00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:15.340
and I have begun watching The Office.

00:00:47.700 --> 00:00:50.640
I like The Office. I am on Team Pam.

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:54.870
I haven't met Karen yet. Definitely. So far I'm

00:00:54.870 --> 00:00:59.280
a fan of Pam. In fact, maybe too much of a

00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:01.770
fan as I've been watching it with

00:01:01.770 --> 00:01:04.229
Catherine and repeatedly telling her how

00:01:04.229 --> 00:01:07.290
a fan I am of Pam. But it's okay, right?

00:01:07.290 --> 00:01:09.960
I mean I can think of four guys right off

00:01:09.960 --> 00:01:11.640
the top of my head that Catherine has

00:01:11.640 --> 00:01:13.710
crushes on that she's never met.

00:01:13.710 --> 00:01:15.240
Eddie Izzard, Christian Bale, Edward Martin,

00:01:15.240 --> 00:01:17.220
Hugh Jackman, Hugh Grant. Wait, was that five?

00:01:17.220 --> 00:01:19.290
Your little building excursion got me

00:01:19.290 --> 00:01:21.119
thinking. It was also my experience with

00:01:21.119 --> 00:01:22.560
a punk rock p-beating. Now a lot of

00:01:22.560 --> 00:01:25.619
people say that as you get older, you get

00:01:25.619 --> 00:01:29.070
smarter, you mature, you start doing less

00:01:29.070 --> 00:01:31.410
stupid things and those same people say

00:01:31.410 --> 00:01:33.060
that young people are stupid. But those

00:01:33.060 --> 00:01:35.160
people must never have met your guide or

00:01:35.160 --> 00:01:37.680
Kurt - the punk rock nerdfighter. Kurt and

00:01:37.680 --> 00:01:39.869
the guide were ready for experiences.

00:01:39.869 --> 00:01:41.610
Things may be a little bit out of the

00:01:41.610 --> 00:01:43.619
ordinary, maybe even a little bit illegal.

00:01:43.619 --> 00:01:46.229
Illegal experiences I do not condone.

00:01:46.229 --> 00:01:48.479
When the opportunity presents itself why

00:01:48.479 --> 00:01:50.340
ignore something new, something

00:01:50.340 --> 00:01:52.800
interesting, something different. But I'm

00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:54.030
proud of you for fighting your fear and

00:01:54.030 --> 00:01:55.649
going ahead and chasing after that

00:01:55.649 --> 00:01:57.810
experience. I'm starting to very

00:01:57.810 --> 00:01:59.369
seriously consider the prospect that as

00:01:59.369 --> 00:02:01.289
you get older, you get stupider

00:02:01.289 --> 00:02:03.959
incrementally, every year, stupider, and

00:02:03.959 --> 00:02:06.929
stupider. What I mean is that maybe you

00:02:06.929 --> 00:02:09.509
have a bad experience or you put your

00:02:09.509 --> 00:02:12.390
values in all the wrong places and you

00:02:12.390 --> 00:02:15.209
end up really consciously avoiding

00:02:15.209 --> 00:02:17.370
anything that might be fun. I mean go to

00:02:17.370 --> 00:02:19.230
any Walmart in America and watch what

00:02:19.230 --> 00:02:21.810
happens. The little kids put things on

00:02:21.810 --> 00:02:24.959
their heads, run around, act silly, do

00:02:24.959 --> 00:02:26.940
stupid things and then their parents are

00:02:26.940 --> 00:02:30.209
like: "Billy, you can't do that in Walmart,

00:02:30.209 --> 00:02:32.400
this is just not the place for having

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:35.040
fun". You know what? I think we should all

00:02:35.040 --> 00:02:37.200
be at Walmart putting stuff on our heads.

00:02:37.200 --> 00:02:38.910
We need to take a cue from the

00:02:38.910 --> 00:02:41.220
four-year-olds of the world.

00:02:41.220 --> 00:02:43.560
Putting things on your head is fun. Fun is good

00:02:43.560 --> 00:02:46.500
for you. There's no Walmart police force

00:02:46.500 --> 00:02:47.760
telling you not to put things on your

00:02:47.760 --> 00:02:49.560
head. More than a dozen people completely

00:02:49.560 --> 00:02:51.060
ignored me when I was sitting on the

00:02:51.060 --> 00:02:52.980
street giving away peeps. What I felt

00:02:52.980 --> 00:02:54.870
like I was saying was here, this is

00:02:54.870 --> 00:02:56.250
something different, something that

00:02:56.250 --> 00:02:57.689
doesn't generally happen to you in your

00:02:57.689 --> 00:02:58.260
normal day.

00:02:58.260 --> 00:03:00.689
Take this strangeness, this experience

00:03:00.689 --> 00:03:03.209
and have some fun with it. Kurt heard me

00:03:03.209 --> 00:03:04.950
loud and clear but that's not what most

00:03:04.950 --> 00:03:06.780
of the people heard. They heard something

00:03:06.780 --> 00:03:09.510
like: "I'm weird and weird people are

00:03:09.510 --> 00:03:12.299
dangerous". If you find yourself getting

00:03:12.299 --> 00:03:15.239
older and less silly, do something about it.

00:03:15.239 --> 00:03:18.480
Put something on your head, do it, put

00:03:18.480 --> 00:03:22.760
it on your head. I'll see you tomorrow.

